"Furthermore, the proliferation of fragmented reporting taxonomies—spanning the EU Corporate Sustainability Reporting Directive ('CSRD'), International Sustainability Standards Board ('ISSB') frameworks, US Securities and Exchange Commission rules, and national industrial-policy disclosures—has created a costly 'compliance duplication burden'. Our internal audit estimates that reconciling overlapping yet non-identical legal, tax, and sustainability filings across thirty-four countries now consumes €68 million annually in external advisory and reporting costs while distracting senior management from core commercial execution.",
