"Effective strategic intelligence differs fundamentally from passive data warehousing or backward-looking financial reporting. While conventional business analytics describes what happened inside the enterprise last quarter, genuine strategic business intelligence operates as an 'anticipatory decision-support system' that fuses open-source intelligence ('OSINT'), patent-citation mapping, scientific publication trajectories, regulatory docket tracking, geopolitical risk modelling, and internal frontline commercial signals into actionable early-warning foresight.",
