"To establish business intelligence as a true pillar of strategic sovereignty at Minerva Aerospace & Defence Systems, this note recommends four institutional measures: first, creating a centralised 'Strategic Foresight & Intelligence Cell' reporting directly to the Chief Executive Officer and Board Strategy Committee without divisional filtering; second, integrating internal frontline sales, procurement, and engineering field observations with external OSINT and patent analytics; third, institutionalising structured 'Red-Team Contrarian Briefings' prior to every major capital allocation or acquisition vote; and fourth, enforcing strict ethical and legal compliance boundaries distinguishing lawful open-source intelligence from illicit corporate espionage.",
